  "explanation": {
    "summary": "な-adjectives are a second kind of describing word. As a predicate (the part at the end of the sentence) they fit the same slot as a noun: [Topic] は [な-adj] です. To make it negative, swap です for じゃないです, the same as with nouns: おとうさんは しずかじゃないです. This is the big difference from い-adjectives. With those you change the word itself (たかい → たかくない). With な-adjectives the word never changes. Only the ending after it changes.",
    "structure_notes": [
      "Slot order: [Topic] + は + [な-adj] + です. The adjective always comes right before です, at the end of the sentence.",
      "Negative: [Topic] は [な-adj] じゃないです. Nothing is added to the adjective itself. You only swap です for じゃないです.",
      "Compare い-adjectives: おいしい → おいしくないです (the word changes). な-adjectives: しずか → しずかじゃないです (the word stays the same).",
      "Questions work as before: add か at the end. おとうさんも げんきですか。 (Is your father well too?)",
      "Watch out: きれい ends in い but is a な-adjective. The negative is きれいじゃないです, never きれくないです."
    ],
    "connects_to": "な-adjectives work exactly like nouns in 〜は〜です and 〜じゃないです (かぞくは しずかじゃないです has the same shape as 私は 学生じゃないです). They are unlike い-adjectives, which change form to 〜くないです."
  },
